 twenty years. He is loved across the nation for his delight in the peculiar and for his ability to find humour and a common ground in all that life brings. The Life and Loves of a He Devil is Graham's funny and honest memoir on the theme of love. As he shows, it's really the things you love that make you who you are and so Graham tells his story from his Irish childhood to the present day, describing just what and who he loved - and sometimes lost - as a young boy, and his new loves and obsessions - big and small - as he's grown older. It's been ten years since his last book and being a decade older Graham has come to realise that what makes a life interesting is less what happens to you and more what inspires and drives you, what you love.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10195197-L.jpg","renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":62,"criticalRenown":48,"controversy":8,"llmAffinity":68,"affinityResidual":-14.37,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.94,"criticalRenown":0.8,"controversy":0.86,"llmAffinity":0.98},"tags":{"craft":"voice","evidence":"personal-experience","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The things people love shape who they become, and what makes life interesting is what inspires and drives them rather than merely what happens to them.","confidence":0.96},"academicOrientation":{"score":25,"confidence":0.95},"profileConfidence":0.98,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"aeb47c135cc340679d04db9748d6be974077abeee2d74eec38deb37383cf251a","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"The Life and Loves of a He Devil is Graham's funny and honest memoir on the theme of love. As he shows, it's really the things you love that make you who you are and so Graham tells his story from his Irish childhood to the present day, describing just what and who he loved - a